{
    "course_code": "CS571",
    "course_title": "Building User Interfaces",
    "credits": "3 credits",
    "course_description": "Introduces software development of user interfaces (UIs). Build competence in implementing UIs using state-of-the-art UI paradigms, methods for capturing, interpreting, and responding to user input, and platform-specific UI development APIs.",
    "course_summary": "Students will learn to implement user interfaces using modern paradigms, capture and interpret user input, and use platform-specific APIs for web, mobile, and desktop applications.",
    "learning_outcomes": "- Program front-end, user-facing software elements using state-of-the-art tools.\n- Engage in design thinking and ideate conceptual design solutions.\n- Prototype and develop user interfaces for various platforms including web and mobile.\n- Follow and apply user-centered design principles and heuristics.\n- Create visual designs and effectually use design languages and elements.",
    "what_you_will_learn": "- Front-end UI programming using modern languages and libraries.\n- Design thinking and conceptual solution communication.\n- Building prototypes for web and mobile UIs.\n- Iterative design and evaluation using user-centered design methods.\n- Visual design, layout, and navigation structure creation.",
